  "_doc": "Crafting recipes (alchemy pills and blacksmith artifacts share these rules and the tunables under alchemy). Success chance = base_chance + rank_bonus * (profession rank - min_rank) + comprehension_step * (the profession's primary attribute - 10, e.g. comprehension for alchemists, constitution for blacksmiths) - difficulty, clamped to [min_chance, max_chance]. A failed refinement destroys all ingredients and gives failure_xp_fraction of the recipe xp. Recipe fields: id, name, profession (a profession id: 'alchemist' for pills, 'blacksmith' for equipment, 'talisman_master' for talismans), ingredients {item_id: count}, output {item, count}, min_rank (profession rank required), days (time one attempt takes), difficulty (subtracted from the chance), xp (profession xp on success), starter (optional bool: known by everyone; other recipes must be learned from an item with the learn_recipe effect, e.g. a recipe scroll), great_output (optional {item, count}: produced instead of output on a great success, e.g. a higher-grade pill). Great success chance = (success chance - great_threshold) * great_scale, clamped to [0, success chance]; it shares the success roll. crafted_sell_markup (>= 1): merchants that buy back a crafted item (any recipe output) pay at most its material cost per unit (ingredient shop prices, cheapest recipe) times this, and never more than the usual half price.",
